{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"linearRegressionY"},{"type":"text","value":" fits numeric y values over a numeric or temporal x channel.\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"linearRegressionX"},{"type":"text","value":" transposes the same semantics to fit numeric x values over\na numeric or temporal y channel. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"linearRegressionRowsY"},{"type":"text","value":" and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"linearRegressionRowsX"},{"type":"text","value":" expose the sampled semantic rows directly."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { linearRegressionY } from '@tanstack/charts/regression'\n\nlinearRegressionY(rows, {\n  x: 'power',\n  y: 'economy',\n  ci: 0.95,\n  stroke: '#dc2626',\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The row transforms and both marks are also exported from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts"},{"type":"text","value":"\nand "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts/universal"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"signatures","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Signatures"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function linearRegressionY<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: LinearRegressionYOptions<TDatum>,\n): ChartMark<LinearRegressionYDatum<TDatum, InferredX>, InferredX, number>\n\nfunction linearRegressionX<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: LinearRegressionXOptions<TDatum>,\n): ChartMark<LinearRegressionXDatum<TDatum, InferredY>, number, InferredY>\n\nfunction linearRegressionRowsY<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: LinearRegressionRowsYOptions<TDatum>,\n): LinearRegressionYDatum<TDatum, InferredX>[]\n\nfunction linearRegressionRowsX<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: LinearRegressionRowsXOptions<TDatum>,\n): LinearRegressionXDatum<TDatum, InferredY>[]","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The independent channel accepts finite numbers or valid "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Date"},{"type":"text","value":" values. The\ndependent channel is numeric. Nullish and non-finite observations are omitted.\nSet "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"z"},{"type":"text","value":" to fit one independent model per first-seen series."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"fit-and-confidence-semantics","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fit and confidence semantics"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each group uses centered ordinary least squares. Centering avoids subtracting\nlarge raw sums and keeps millisecond "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Date"},{"type":"text","value":" values stable. Groups with fewer\nthan two valid observations or no independent variance are omitted."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The confidence band describes the fitted mean, using a Student-t critical\nvalue and residual degrees of freedom. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ci"},{"type":"text","value":" defaults to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0.95"},{"type":"text","value":"; set it to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0"},{"type":"text","value":"\nto omit the band. A two-point fit has no residual degrees of freedom, so it\nrenders the line without a band."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"samples"},{"type":"text","value":" controls the number of evenly spaced values across the observed\nsemantic independent domain. It defaults to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"64"},{"type":"text","value":" and must be an integer of at\nleast two. This is deliberately not a pixel precision: changing chart size\ndoes not change the model data or motion identity. Multiple samples also keep\nthe fitted path faithful when the independent scale is nonlinear."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"eager-rows","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Eager rows"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use the row transforms when fitted values feed more than the convenience\nmark:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { linearRegressionRowsY } from '@tanstack/charts/regression'\n\nconst fitted = linearRegressionRowsY(rows, {\n  x: 'date',\n  y: 'value',\n  z: 'series',\n  samples: 32,\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"y"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"z"},{"type":"text","value":" use the standard "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TransformValue"},{"type":"text","value":" contract. Accessors receive\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ datum, index, data }"},{"type":"text","value":". The transform runs eagerly, does not mutate source\nrows, omits invalid and unfittable groups, and returns only semantic samples\nand lineage. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"linearRegressionY"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"linearRegressionX"},{"type":"text","value":" add presentation\nidentity when composing the confidence area and fitted line."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Option"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Meaning"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"id"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Layer-derived"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stable composite mark ID"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Orientation-specific "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Channel"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Numeric dependent or number/Date independent data"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"y"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Orientation-specific "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Channel"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Numeric dependent or number/Date independent data"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"z"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Channel<TDatum, ChartKey?>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"One group"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Independent fit series"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ci"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"},{"type":"text","value":" in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"[0, 1)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0.95"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fitted-mean confidence level; "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0"},{"type":"text","value":" hides the band"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"samples"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Integer"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"64"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Semantic-domain samples per fit"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stroke"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Series color"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Regression-line paint"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"strokeOpacity"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SVG default"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Regression-line opacity"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"strokeWidth"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"1.5"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Regression-line width"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"strokeDasharray"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Regression-line dash pattern"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fill"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Line stroke"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Confidence-band paint"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fillOpacity"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0.1"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Confidence-band opacity"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"motion"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartMotionDefinition<LinearRegression*Datum<...>>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Motion over derived samples"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"derived-data-and-lineage","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Derived data and lineage"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each interactive line sample contains its semantic independent value, fitted\nvalue, optional confidence bounds, group, and aggregate lineage:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"interface LinearRegressionYDatum<TDatum, TXValue> {\n  x: TXValue\n  y: number\n  y1?: number\n  y2?: number\n  group: ChartKey | null\n  source: readonly TDatum[]\n  sourceIndexes: readonly number[]\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"LinearRegressionXDatum"},{"type":"text","value":" transposes these fields to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x"},{"type":"text","value":", optional "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x1"},{"type":"text","value":" and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x2"},{"type":"text","value":", and independent "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"y"},{"type":"text","value":". Lineage contains only finite observations that\ncontributed to that group's fit, in source order."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The public option types are "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"LinearRegressionRowsYOptions"},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"LinearRegressionRowsXOptions"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"LinearRegressionYOptions"},{"type":"text","value":", and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"LinearRegressionXOptions"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The confidence area and fitted line are ordinary "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"areaY"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"areaX"},{"type":"text","value":" and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lineY"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lineX"},{"type":"text","value":" children. Only the fitted line contributes interaction points;\nthe band is decorative. This prevents a tooltip or focus step from receiving\nduplicate targets for the same fitted sample."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"signatures","text":"Signatures","level":2},{"id":"fit-and-confidence-semantics","text":"Fit and confidence semantics","level":2},{"id":"eager-rows","text":"Eager rows","level":2},{"id":"options","text":"Options","level":2},{"id":"derived-data-and-lineage","text":"Derived data and lineage","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n`linearRegressionY` fits numeric y values over a numeric or temporal x channel.\n`linearRegressionX` transposes the same semantics to fit numeric x values over\na numeric or temporal y channel. `linearRegressionRowsY` and\n`linearRegressionRowsX` expose the sampled semantic rows directly.\n\n```ts\nimport { linearRegressionY } from '@tanstack/charts/regression'\n\nlinearRegressionY(rows, {\n  x: 'power',\n  y: 'economy',\n  ci: 0.95,\n  stroke: '#dc2626',\n})\n```\n\nThe row transforms and both marks are also exported from `@tanstack/charts`\nand `@tanstack/charts/universal`.\n\n## Signatures\n\n```ts\nfunction linearRegressionY<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: LinearRegressionYOptions<TDatum>,\n): ChartMark<LinearRegressionYDatum<TDatum, InferredX>, InferredX, number>\n\nfunction linearRegressionX<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: LinearRegressionXOptions<TDatum>,\n): ChartMark<LinearRegressionXDatum<TDatum, InferredY>, number, InferredY>\n\nfunction linearRegressionRowsY<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: LinearRegressionRowsYOptions<TDatum>,\n): LinearRegressionYDatum<TDatum, InferredX>[]\n\nfunction linearRegressionRowsX<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: LinearRegressionRowsXOptions<TDatum>,\n): LinearRegressionXDatum<TDatum, InferredY>[]\n```\n\nThe independent channel accepts finite numbers or valid `Date` values. The\ndependent channel is numeric. Nullish and non-finite observations are omitted.\nSet `z` to fit one independent model per first-seen series.\n\n## Fit and confidence semantics\n\nEach group uses centered ordinary least squares. Centering avoids subtracting\nlarge raw sums and keeps millisecond `Date` values stable. Groups with fewer\nthan two valid observations or no independent variance are omitted.\n\nThe confidence band describes the fitted mean, using a Student-t critical\nvalue and residual degrees of freedom. `ci` defaults to `0.95`; set it to `0`\nto omit the band. A two-point fit has no residual degrees of freedom, so it\nrenders the line without a band.\n\n`samples` controls the number of evenly spaced values across the observed\nsemantic independent domain. It defaults to `64` and must be an integer of at\nleast two. This is deliberately not a pixel precision: changing chart size\ndoes not change the model data or motion identity. Multiple samples also keep\nthe fitted path faithful when the independent scale is nonlinear.\n\n## Eager rows\n\nUse the row transforms when fitted values feed more than the convenience\nmark:\n\n```ts\nimport { linearRegressionRowsY } from '@tanstack/charts/regression'\n\nconst fitted = linearRegressionRowsY(rows, {\n  x: 'date',\n  y: 'value',\n  z: 'series',\n  samples: 32,\n})\n```\n\n`x`, `y`, and `z` use the standard `TransformValue` contract. Accessors receive\n`{ datum, index, data }`. The transform runs eagerly, does not mutate source\nrows, omits invalid and unfittable groups, and returns only semantic samples\nand lineage. `linearRegressionY` and `linearRegressionX` add presentation\nidentity when composing the confidence area and fitted line.\n\n## Options\n\n| Option            | Type                                                 | Default       | Meaning                                           |\n| ----------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- | ------------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `id`              | `string`                                             | Layer-derived | Stable composite mark ID                          |\n| `x`               | Orientation-specific `Channel`                       | Required      | Numeric dependent or number/Date independent data |\n| `y`               | Orientation-specific `Channel`                       | Required      | Numeric dependent or number/Date independent data |\n| `z`               | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey?>`                         | One group     | Independent fit series                            |\n| `ci`              | `number` in `[0, 1)`                                 | `0.95`        | Fitted-mean confidence level; `0` hides the band  |\n| `samples`         | Integer                                              | `64`          | Semantic-domain samples per fit                   |\n| `stroke`          | `string`                                             | Series color  | Regression-line paint                             |\n| `strokeOpacity`   | `number`                                             | SVG default   | Regression-line opacity                           |\n| `strokeWidth`     | `number`                                             | `1.5`         | Regression-line width                             |\n| `strokeDasharray` | `string`                                             | None          | Regression-line dash pattern                      |\n| `fill`            | `string`                                             | Line stroke   | Confidence-band paint                             |\n| `fillOpacity`     | `number`                                             | `0.1`         | Confidence-band opacity                           |\n| `motion`          | `ChartMotionDefinition<LinearRegression*Datum<...>>` | None          | Motion over derived samples                       |\n\n## Derived data and lineage\n\nEach interactive line sample contains its semantic independent value, fitted\nvalue, optional confidence bounds, group, and aggregate lineage:\n\n```ts\ninterface LinearRegressionYDatum<TDatum, TXValue> {\n  x: TXValue\n  y: number\n  y1?: number\n  y2?: number\n  group: ChartKey | null\n  source: readonly TDatum[]\n  sourceIndexes: readonly number[]\n}\n```\n\n`LinearRegressionXDatum` transposes these fields to `x`, optional `x1` and\n`x2`, and independent `y`. Lineage contains only finite observations that\ncontributed to that group's fit, in source order.\n\nThe public option types are `LinearRegressionRowsYOptions`,\n`LinearRegressionRowsXOptions`, `LinearRegressionYOptions`, and\n`LinearRegressionXOptions`.\n\nThe confidence area and fitted line are ordinary `areaY`/`areaX` and\n`lineY`/`lineX` children. Only the fitted line contributes interaction points;\nthe band is decorative. This prevents a tooltip or focus step from receiving\nduplicate targets for the same fitted sample.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Linear Regression Marks\ndescription: Reference for eager linearRegressionRowsY/X data and linearRegressionY/X least-squares marks, confidence bands, grouping, sampling, lineage, and interaction.\n---\n\n`linearRegressionY` fits numeric y values over a numeric or temporal x channel.\n`linearRegressionX` transposes the same semantics to fit numeric x values over\na numeric or temporal y channel. `linearRegressionRowsY` and\n`linearRegressionRowsX` expose the sampled semantic rows directly.\n\n```ts\nimport { linearRegressionY } from '@tanstack/charts/regression'\n\nlinearRegressionY(rows, {\n  x: 'power',\n  y: 'economy',\n  ci: 0.95,\n  stroke: '#dc2626',\n})\n```\n\nThe row transforms and both marks are also exported from `@tanstack/charts`\nand `@tanstack/charts/universal`.\n\n## Signatures\n\n```ts\nfunction linearRegressionY<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: LinearRegressionYOptions<TDatum>,\n): ChartMark<LinearRegressionYDatum<TDatum, InferredX>, InferredX, number>\n\nfunction linearRegressionX<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: LinearRegressionXOptions<TDatum>,\n): ChartMark<LinearRegressionXDatum<TDatum, InferredY>, number, InferredY>\n\nfunction linearRegressionRowsY<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: LinearRegressionRowsYOptions<TDatum>,\n): LinearRegressionYDatum<TDatum, InferredX>[]\n\nfunction linearRegressionRowsX<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: LinearRegressionRowsXOptions<TDatum>,\n): LinearRegressionXDatum<TDatum, InferredY>[]\n```\n\nThe independent channel accepts finite numbers or valid `Date` values. The\ndependent channel is numeric. Nullish and non-finite observations are omitted.\nSet `z` to fit one independent model per first-seen series.\n\n## Fit and confidence semantics\n\nEach group uses centered ordinary least squares. Centering avoids subtracting\nlarge raw sums and keeps millisecond `Date` values stable. Groups with fewer\nthan two valid observations or no independent variance are omitted.\n\nThe confidence band describes the fitted mean, using a Student-t critical\nvalue and residual degrees of freedom. `ci` defaults to `0.95`; set it to `0`\nto omit the band. A two-point fit has no residual degrees of freedom, so it\nrenders the line without a band.\n\n`samples` controls the number of evenly spaced values across the observed\nsemantic independent domain. It defaults to `64` and must be an integer of at\nleast two. This is deliberately not a pixel precision: changing chart size\ndoes not change the model data or motion identity. Multiple samples also keep\nthe fitted path faithful when the independent scale is nonlinear.\n\n## Eager rows\n\nUse the row transforms when fitted values feed more than the convenience\nmark:\n\n```ts\nimport { linearRegressionRowsY } from '@tanstack/charts/regression'\n\nconst fitted = linearRegressionRowsY(rows, {\n  x: 'date',\n  y: 'value',\n  z: 'series',\n  samples: 32,\n})\n```\n\n`x`, `y`, and `z` use the standard `TransformValue` contract. Accessors receive\n`{ datum, index, data }`. The transform runs eagerly, does not mutate source\nrows, omits invalid and unfittable groups, and returns only semantic samples\nand lineage. `linearRegressionY` and `linearRegressionX` add presentation\nidentity when composing the confidence area and fitted line.\n\n## Options\n\n| Option            | Type                                                 | Default       | Meaning                                           |\n| ----------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- | ------------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `id`              | `string`                                             | Layer-derived | Stable composite mark ID                          |\n| `x`               | Orientation-specific `Channel`                       | Required      | Numeric dependent or number/Date independent data |\n| `y`               | Orientation-specific `Channel`                       | Required      | Numeric dependent or number/Date independent data |\n| `z`               | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey?>`                         | One group     | Independent fit series                            |\n| `ci`              | `number` in `[0, 1)`                                 | `0.95`        | Fitted-mean confidence level; `0` hides the band  |\n| `samples`         | Integer                                              | `64`          | Semantic-domain samples per fit                   |\n| `stroke`          | `string`                                             | Series color  | Regression-line paint                             |\n| `strokeOpacity`   | `number`                                             | SVG default   | Regression-line opacity                           |\n| `strokeWidth`     | `number`                                             | `1.5`         | Regression-line width                             |\n| `strokeDasharray` | `string`                                             | None          | Regression-line dash pattern                      |\n| `fill`            | `string`                                             | Line stroke   | Confidence-band paint                             |\n| `fillOpacity`     | `number`                                             | `0.1`         | Confidence-band opacity                           |\n| `motion`          | `ChartMotionDefinition<LinearRegression*Datum<...>>` | None          | Motion over derived samples                       |\n\n## Derived data and lineage\n\nEach interactive line sample contains its semantic independent value, fitted\nvalue, optional confidence bounds, group, and aggregate lineage:\n\n```ts\ninterface LinearRegressionYDatum<TDatum, TXValue> {\n  x: TXValue\n  y: number\n  y1?: number\n  y2?: number\n  group: ChartKey | null\n  source: readonly TDatum[]\n  sourceIndexes: readonly number[]\n}\n```\n\n`LinearRegressionXDatum` transposes these fields to `x`, optional `x1` and\n`x2`, and independent `y`. Lineage contains only finite observations that\ncontributed to that group's fit, in source order.\n\nThe public option types are `LinearRegressionRowsYOptions`,\n`LinearRegressionRowsXOptions`, `LinearRegressionYOptions`, and\n`LinearRegressionXOptions`.\n\nThe confidence area and fitted line are ordinary `areaY`/`areaX` and\n`lineY`/`lineX` children. Only the fitted line contributes interaction points;\nthe band is decorative. This prevents a tooltip or focus step from receiving\nduplicate targets for the same fitted sample.\n"}
